      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "H2L (0.3 mmol, 115.4 mg) was suspended in EtOH (15 mL) and anhydrous ZnCl2 (0.3 mmol, 40.8 mg) was added. The mixture was ultrasonicated for 5 min until fully dissolved, then DyCl3·6H2O (0.15 mmol, 56.5 mg) was added. After addition of Et3N (0.6 mmol, 84 μL) the solution became colorless and transparent. After stirring for a few minutes the solution was filtered; the filtrate was placed at the bottom of a tube and layered with diethyl ether. Colorless multishaped crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction were collected after about 3 days. Λ and Δ enantiomers form by spontaneous resolution.",
        "reagents": [
